From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YANG JOO WOONG <yjw.cpa@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 05 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu/gmc12: widen DMA mask from 44 to 48 bit

RDNA4 (gfx1201) sets a 44-bit DMA mask via gmc_v12_0_sw_init().
On X99 platforms (Broadwell-EP) the BIOS maps GPU BARs above 44-bit
(e.g. 0x380000000000 ≈ 46 bit).  With iommu=pt the IOMMU performs no
address translation, so amdgpu_device_is_peer_accessible() compares
the raw BAR address against the DMA mask and rejects P2P because
46 > 44.

Widening to 48 bit (256 TB) covers all practical BAR placements while
staying well within the GPU's internal VA width.  The GART/VMPT page
tables are unaffected — they already use a 44-bit MC mask
(AMDGPU_GMC_HOLE_MASK) which is independent of the DMA mask.

Tested: dual Radeon AI PRO R9700 (gfx1201) on E5-2699v4 + X99-E WS,
BARs at 0x380000000000 and 0x3C0000000000, iommu=pt restored.
hipDeviceCanAccessPeer() returns 1, hipMemcpyPeer 10.2 GB/s through
PLX PEX8747.

Signed-off-by: YANG JOO WOONG <yjw.cpa@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v12_0.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v12_0.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v12_0.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v12_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v12_0.c
@@ -914,12 +914,12 @@ static int gmc_v12_0_sw_init(struct amdgpu_ip_block *ip_block)
 	adev->gmc.mc_mask = AMDGPU_GMC_HOLE_MASK;

-	r = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(adev->dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(44));
+	r = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(adev->dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(48));
 	if (r) {
 		drm_warn(adev_to_drm(adev), "No suitable DMA available.\n");
 		return r;
 	}

-	adev->need_swiotlb = drm_need_swiotlb(44);
+	adev->need_swiotlb = drm_need_swiotlb(48);

 	r = gmc_v12_0_mc_init(adev);
